From a8c45ad7f176f0ba833fe5feee0fb5d96fecb76b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:27:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] The field equations of forwardLoopCfg and rulerHostCfg;
 pairEncode_drop; spaceUsedByTape_eq_card

For U2's universal machines (megafill C's review of the U2 brief, Q-U1, F1, F2):
- Build/StepBlockForward, Build/InputDevice: simps field equations (not
  simp lemmas) for Turing.StepBlock.forwardLoopCfg and Turing.rulerHostCfg;
- Build/InputDevice: Turing.pairEncode_drop, the payload after one pairing's
  header, with pairEncode_pairEncode_drop re-proved through it (its local copy
  had unfolded pairEncode);
- Deterministic: Turing.MultiTapeTM.spaceUsedByTape_eq_card, a tape's space as
  the count of the cells its head visited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
